  "id": "useful-field-of-view",
  "term": "useful field of view",
  "definition": "Useful field of view is the area of the visual field from which a person can take in information in a single glance without moving the eyes or head. In psychology and vision research, it refers to how efficiently someone can quickly pick out relevant visual information, a skill linked to everyday activities such as driving, visual search, and mobility.",
